$DIR/main.p:23:2: cannot pass &buf to (*O).Drop, which keeps it after returning
    &buf points into buf. buf is a local array of f (declared at main.p:21).
    (*O).Drop stores o in package variable keep (main.p:17), so &buf would
    outlive buf.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    If (*O).Drop should keep its own copy of buf, change it to take the value,
    not a pointer, or an owner it can keep: an owned[[2]int] from new, a
    shared[[2]int], or a library owner such as a vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3003" for a longer explanation)
